@mainpage
The @b µTest++ project is a C++20 testing framework for embedded systems,
which also runs on the native platforms. The tests are ordinary C++ code,
with no preprocessor macros, organised in test suites and test cases.

The results are written in the
[TAP](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Test_Anything_Protocol)
(Test Anything Protocol) format by default, which the continuous
integration systems and the TAP tools read. A human-readable format is
also available, for reading the results on the console.

The command-line options select the format, how much is displayed (from
nothing, with only the exit code, to every check), the colours, an output
file, and the test cases to run.

@section mainpage-start Getting started

The applications include a single header, `micro-os-plus/micro-test-plus.h`.
The header declares nothing unless the macro
`MICRO_OS_PLUS_MICRO_TEST_PLUS_ENABLED` is defined, preferably in
`micro-os-plus/micro-test-plus-defines.h`, for the application and for
the library sources (see @ref micro-os-plus-micro-test-plus-config).

A complete test program has a runner, initialised with the command-line
arguments, a top suite created in `main()` (optional, since the suites can
be added to the runner instead), test cases with checks, and returns the
exit code of the session:

@code{.cpp}
#include <micro-os-plus/micro-test-plus.h>

namespace mt = micro_os_plus::micro_test_plus;

mt::runner tr;

int
main (int argc, char* argv[])
{
  tr.initialise (argc, argv);

  auto& ts = tr.add_top_suite ();

  ts.test ("Check truth", [] (auto& t) {
    t.expect (mt::eq (6 * 7, 42)) << "the answer is 42";
  });

  return tr.run_suites ();
}
@endcode

The topics of the @ref micro-os-plus-micro-test-plus-cpp-api group
describe the runner, the suites, the test cases, and the checks, and the
@ref micro-os-plus-micro-test-plus-cli group the options of the test
programs. The main classes are
@ref micro_os_plus::micro_test_plus::runner "runner",
@ref micro_os_plus::micro_test_plus::runner_options "runner_options",
@ref micro_os_plus::micro_test_plus::suite "suite", and
@ref micro_os_plus::micro_test_plus::test_case "test_case". The installation, the first project, and the user manual are
in the
<a href="../getting-started/">Getting Started</a>
and
<a href="../user/">User's Guide</a>
pages of the site.
